# What travels in the sdist beyond the package itself.
#
# The wheel is settled by `tool.setuptools.package-data` in pyproject.toml,
# and tests/test_packaging.py guards it. This file governs the sdist, where
# the bar is different: an sdist should be able to build and verify itself.
# Until this was measured it could do neither. setuptools swept tests/*.py
# in on its own but left behind conftest.py, tests/__init__.py and
# tests/corpus.py, so `pytest` in an unpacked sdist stopped on 20 collection
# errors -- no ipa fixture, no tests.corpus, no scripts/ to import from --
# without running one test. None of that is visible from a checkout, where
# the files are on disk whether they ship or not.
#
# Each line below is here because something breaks without it.

include CHANGELOG.md
include Makefile

# conftest.py holds the session-scoped ipa and mapper fixtures nearly every
# test takes, and tests/__init__.py is what makes `tests.corpus` -- the one
# canonical corpus enumeration -- importable as a module.
include conftest.py
recursive-include tests *.py

# Not dev-only clutter. test_notation.py and test_zero.py put scripts/ on
# sys.path and import from it; `make check` runs invariants.py, confusion.py,
# xsampa_table.py, tutorial.py, docexamples.py and docquotes.py as release
# gates; and
# `make figures` runs tract_svg.py, which is a shim over ipakit.tract_svg --
# the renderer itself ships in the package, because it has to reach an
# installed user and nothing under scripts/ does.
recursive-include scripts *.py

# docs/tutorial.md is where a newcomer is sent, and `make check` regenerates
# it from tutorial.src.md and compares -- which needs both files present.
# The figures are checked in so a reader gets them without running anything;
# that should hold for a reader who unpacked the sdist too.
recursive-include docs *.md
recursive-include docs *.svg
